{"name":"Bon Vivant","hex":"#5e496a","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bon vivant","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A man who enjoys luxurious things in life, especially good food and drink; a man about town."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bon_vivant"}],"entries":[{"title":"1971 Bon Vivant botulism incident","blocks":[{"text":"In 1971, a married couple in the U.S. state of New York consumed a can of vichyssoise soup made by the company Bon Vivant. The soup was contaminated with botulism toxin, resulting in the man's death and the woman's temporary paralysis. A recall of the soup cans later took place. The company also went out of business in the following three years."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/1971_Bon_Vivant_botulism_incident"},{"title":"Bon","blocks":[{"text":"Bon or Bön, also known as Yungdrung Bon, is the indigenous Tibetan religion which shares many similarities and influences with Tibetan Buddhism but retains elements from earlier Tibetan religious traditions. Bon is a significant minority religion in Tibet, especially in the east, as well as in the surrounding Himalayan regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg/330px-Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bon"},{"title":"Vivant","blocks":[{"text":"Vivant is a small social-liberal political party in Belgium founded by millionaire Roland Duchâtelet. In the regional elections in June 2004, the party formed a strategic alliance with the Flemish Liberals and Democrats (VLD). Both parties are founded on the principle of individualism and can be called liberal. In 2007, the party announced it would likely merge with the VLD."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vivant"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg/250px-Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg/250px-Bon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An advertisement for Bon Vivant vichyssoise cream soup","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABon_Vivant_vichyssoise_advertisement.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg/500px-Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg/500px-Narshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bon monastery of Nangzhik Gompa in Ngawa, Sichuan, China","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANarshi_Gonpa_Ngawa_Sichuan_China.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg/330px-Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg/330px-Tonpa_Shenrab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A statue of Tonpa Shenrab, the central Buddha in Yungdrung Bon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATonpa_Shenrab.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikip